{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GuB3Asdh84rfEPkUcaETs2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — configuration surface table (Phase A)\n2\t\n3\tDerived mechanically from `c_src/include/mujs.h` (public API), `c_src/src/jsi.h`\n4\t(internal API + enums + limits), `c_src/src/regexp.h`, `c_src/src/utf.h` and the\n5\t`if` / `switch` branches the C actually takes on each flag.\n6\t\n7\t## Build-time configuration\n8\t\n9\t`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section**, and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no\n10\t`option()` / `-D` switches (it globs `src/*.c`, one `SHARED` target, `-w`).\n11\tTherefore the complete set of valid feature combinations is:\n12\t\n13\t| # | combination | cargo invocation |\n14\t|---|-------------|------------------|\n15\t| 1 | *(default = empty feature set)* | `cargo test --no-default-features` (identical to `cargo test`) |\n16\t\n17\tThere is no binary/driver target: `regexp.c`'s `main()` is behind `#ifdef TEST`,\n18\twhich CMake never defines, and `[lib] crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` is the only Rust\n19\ttarget. So the \"compare C and Rust binary stdout\" gate is N/A.\n20\t\n21\t## Runtime configuration axes (from the C source)\n22\t\n23\t| axis | values the C branches on | where |\n24\t|------|--------------------------|-------|\n25\t| `js_newstate` flags | `0`, `JS_STRICT`(1), and out-of-range bits (e.g. `2`, `-1`, `0x7fffffff`) — only bit 0 is read: `if (flags & JS_STRICT) J->strict = J->default_strict = 1` | jsstate.c:196 |\n26\t| `js_newstate` alloc | `NULL` (→ `js_defaultalloc` = realloc/free), custom allocator, allocator that fails | jsstate.c:180-190 |\n27\t| `js_setlimit` | `runlimit` 0 (off) / 1 / N; `memlimit` 0 (off) / small / large | jsrun.c:46-76, 1602 |\n28\t| report callback | default (`fputs` to stderr) or user `js_Report` | jsstate.c:24, 160 |\n29\t| panic handler | default (`js_report \"uncaught exception\"`) or user `js_Panic` | jsstate.c:29, 152 |\n30\t| script vs eval | `js_loadstring` (uses `J->default_strict`) vs `js_loadeval` (uses `J->strict`, inherits env `J->E` when strict) | jsstate.c:110-125 |\n31\t| property attributes | cross product of `JS_READONLY`(1) `JS_DONTENUM`(2) `JS_DONTCONF`(4) = 8 | mujs.h, jsrun.c jsR_defproperty |\n32\t| RegExp flags (JS level) | cross product of `JS_REGEXP_G`(1) `JS_REGEXP_I`(2) `JS_REGEXP_M`(4) = 8 | jsregexp.c |\n33\t| `regcomp` cflags | cross product `REG_ICASE`(1) `REG_NEWLINE`(2) = 4, plus out-of-range bits | regexp.c regcompx |\n34\t| `regexec` eflags | `0`, `REG_NOTBOL`(4), plus out-of-range bits | regexp.c regexec |\n35\t| `js_pushiterator` own | `0` (walk prototype chain) / `1` (own properties only) | jsproperty.c jsV_newiterator |\n36\t| userdata kind | `js_newuserdata` (finalize only) vs `js_newuserdatax` (has/put/delete/finalize) | jsvalue.c |\n37\t| cfunction kind | `js_newcfunction` / `js_newcfunctionx` (data+finalize) / `js_newcconstructor` | jsvalue.c |\n38\t| string representation | `JS_TSHRSTR` (≤ 15 bytes, inline), `JS_TLITSTR` (interned/literal), `JS_TMEMSTR` (heap, refcounted) | jsi.h:302, jsrun.c js_pushstring/js_pushlstring/js_pushliteral |\n39\t| object class | 16 values of `enum js_Class` (`JS_COBJECT`..`JS_CUSERDATA`) | jsi.h:313 |\n40\t| value type | 8 values of `enum js_Type` | jsi.h:302 |\n41\t| array representation | flat/`simple` (`u.a.array`) vs unflattened property list (`jsV_unflattenarray`); `flat_length` vs `length`; sparse | jsproperty.c, jsrun.c jsR_setarrayindex |\n42\t| number shape | `+0`, `-0`, NaN, ±Inf, integers, denormals, `1e21` boundary (`jsV_numbertostring` switch), radix 2..36 | jsvalue.c, jsdtoa.c |\n43\t| UTF-8 shape | 1/2/3/4-byte sequences, invalid lead/continuation bytes, overlong forms, surrogates, `Runemax` | utf.c |\n44\t| `js_gc` report | `0` (silent) / non-zero (prints stats with `printf`) | jsgc.c |\n45\t| `TZ` environment | affects `LocalTZA` / `DaylightSavingTA` (`localtime`/`mktime`) | jsdate.c |\n46\t| JSON options | `JSON.parse` with/without reviver; `JSON.stringify` with replacer function / replacer array / `undefined`; indent number 0..10 / string / `undefined` | json.c |\n47\t\n48\t## Configuration rows to verify\n49\t\n50\tEvery row is exercised through the `.so` exports of BOTH libraries with many\n51\trandomized inputs (fixed seed) and the outputs compared byte-for-byte.\n52\t\n53\t### A. `utf.c` — lowest level, no `js_State`\n54\t\n55\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n56\t|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n57\t| A1 | `jsU_chartorune` | all 1-byte inputs `0x01..0x7F` (ASCII fast path) | [x] |\n58\t| A2 | `jsU_chartorune` | `0x00` (empty string / NUL terminator) | [x] |\n59\t| A3 | `jsU_chartorune` | every well-formed 2-byte sequence (`0xC0..0xDF` + cont) | [x] |\n60\t| A4 | `jsU_chartorune` | every well-formed 3-byte sequence, incl. surrogate range `D800..DFFF` | [x] |\n61\t| A5 | `jsU_chartorune` | every well-formed 4-byte sequence up to `Runemax` and past it | [x] |\n62\t| A6 | `jsU_chartorune` | invalid lead byte `0x80..0xBF` (bare continuation) | [x] |\n63\t| A7 | `jsU_chartorune` | truncated sequences (lead byte then NUL / then non-continuation) | [x] |\n64\t| A8 | `jsU_chartorune` | overlong encodings (`C0 80`, `E0 80 80`, `F0 80 80 80`) | [x] |\n65\t| A9 | `jsU_chartorune` | lead bytes `0xF8..0xFF` (5/6-byte / invalid) | [x] |\n66\t| A10 | `jsU_chartorune` | exhaustive sweep of all 3-byte and randomized 4-byte byte strings | [x] |\n67\t| A11 | `jsU_runetochar` | every rune `0..0x110000+` incl. negatives, `Runeerror`, `Runemax`, `Runemax+1` | [x] |\n68\t| A12 | `jsU_runelen` | every rune `-1000..0x110100` | [x] |\n69\t| A13 | `jsU_runetochar`→`jsU_chartorune` | round-trip over all runes | [x] |\n70\t| A14 | `jsU_isalpharune` / `islowerrune` / `isupperrune` | exhaustive `0..0x110000` (binary-search tables in utfdata.h) | [x] |\n71\t| A15 | `jsU_tolowerrune` / `jsU_toupperrune` | exhaustive `0..0x110000`