{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_a754bah7xuz7e6kn6y7v2zxgt6mgkaqskxbgvv5qh5cxvybt67dq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `tests/scripts_core.rs` is the only file I created or touched.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`#[test]` functions:** 10 (`h1_operators`, `h2_statements`, `h3_functions`, `h4_object_builtins`, `h5_array_builtins`, `h6_array_sort`, `h7_string_builtins`, `h8_number_builtins`, `h9_math_builtins`, `h10_boolean_and_function_methods`) — CONFIGS.md rows H1..H10.\n\n**Total scripts in the corpus: 971** (928 literal scripts + 43 generated in H9 from the `Math` function × argument-set cross product). Per test: H1 110, H2 121, H3 90, H4 113, H5 136, H6 61, H7 113, H8 72, H9 79, H10 77. Most run under both sloppy and strict (`diff_scripts_both_modes`), so ~1900 script executions per library; `with` (H2), `arguments.callee` (H3) and the sloppy-vs-strict silent-write cases (H4) are pinned to a single mode.\n\n**Result: 9 passed, 1 failed** (stable across 4 full runs).\n\n**No crashes.** The whole corpus was pre-screened against both shared objects with a standalone C driver before being committed, and nothing segfaults or aborts; the `// CRASHES:` list at the bottom of the file is therefore empty.\n\n### Failing test: `h9_math_builtins` — 2 diverging scripts (same root cause, reproduces in *both* flags=0 and JS_STRICT)\n\n```\n[27] var V=[-0,0,0.5,-0.5,1,-1,2,-2,0.1,1e300,-1e300,1e-300,NaN,Infinity,-Infinity,Math.PI,Math.E,1e21,-1e21];\n     function show(t,x){ print(t, x.toString(), 1/x); }\n     function one(nm,f){ for (var i=0;i<V.length;i++) show(nm+'('+V[i]+')', f(V[i])); }\n     one(\"round\", function(x){ return Math.round(x); });\n  C   : rc=0  ... round(-0.5) 0 Infinity ...      (all 19 other lines identical)\n  Rust: rc=0  ... round(-0.5) 0 -Infinity ...\n\n[60] print(Math.round(0.5), Math.round(-0.5), 1/Math.round(-0.5), Math.round(1.5), Math.round(-1.5), Math.round(2.5));\n  C   : rc=0 out=\"1 0 Infinity 2 -1 3\\n\"\n  Rust: rc=0 out=\"1 0 -Infinity 2 -1 3\\n\"\n```\n\n**Root cause (a real translation bug, left in place as instructed):** `jsM_round` in `c_src/src/jsmath.c` ends its negative branch with `return -0;`. In C that is the *integer* constant `0` negated — still integer `0` — which converts to `+0.0`. `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hWAEAP/translated_rust/src/jsmath.rs:28` translated it as the floating literal `-0.0`, which genuinely is negative zero. So for `-0.5 <= x < 0` the C `Math.round` yields `+0` and Rust yields `-0`. The faithful fix is `return 0.0;` in `src/jsmath.rs`. I verified by sweeping all 79 H9 scripts through both libraries in strict mode as well — this is the only divergence hiding behind the panic.\n\n### One harness issue worth flagging (documented in a footer comment, not a translation bug)\n\n`print.toString()` cannot be used in this corpus. `js_newcfunctionx` (`c_src/src/jsvalue.c`) stores its `name` argument as a bare pointer (`obj->u.c.name = name;`) without copying, while `tests/common/mod.rs:628` registers the global with `cs(\"print\").as_ptr()` — a `CString` temporary that is dropped at the end of that statement. `Function.prototype.toString` on `print` therefore reads freed heap and prints different garbage in each library and on each run (I hit this once: `function pY\\u{1}0…()` vs `function \\u{10}|\\u{1}0…()`). That is a use-after-free in the harness, so H10 exercises `Function.prototype.toString` against `Math.max`, `Object.keys`, `Array.prototype.slice`, `JSON.stringify` and `Number.prototype.toFixed` instead. I did not modify `tests/common/mod.rs`.\n\nAlso note `debugger;` (H2) makes both libraries dump the VM stack to **stderr**, which the harness does not capture — those dumps appear in the test log but are not compared, and H2 passes.\n\n### Things confirmed against the C source rather than assumed\n- No `fn.name` property exists in this MuJS (H3 asserts `f.name === undefined` / `\"name\" in f === false`).\n- No `String.prototype.substr` and no `Array.prototype.toLocaleString` (H7 probes `substr`'s absence explicitly, wrapped in try/catch).\n- `Ap_sort` has **no** insertion-sort/heapsort threshold in this version — it shortcuts only at `len <= 1` and otherwise always runs `Ap_sort_heapsort`; H6 still covers 0/1/2/3/16/17/18/33/64/200 elements plus the `simple`/flat vs. sparse branches of `Ap_sort_swap`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":130442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1122,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019WMd9TjfscpAoEgBRzf7iE","session_id":"f3ff8386-8592-4dbd-8b83-c0778c2e2173","uuid":"57eeff61-257a-4cd1-ae75-c04ba92fb2a6","timestamp":"2026-08-14T19:54:18.534Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write script corpus tests part 1"}
