{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4dpygcrdor4xbamasfn2ch5ni2xd635e4po5lyurcjxq42qviqjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. One new file written: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hWAEAP/translated_rust/tests/numbers.rs` (nothing else modified).\n\n## Result (verbatim, final run of `cargo test --test numbers`)\n\n```\nrunning 11 tests\ntest c4b_fmtexp_out_of_range_exponent_subprocess ... ignored\ntest c4_fmtexp_all_exponents ... ok\ntest c1_strtod_corpus ... ok\ntest c2_strtod_overflow_underflow_and_maxexponent ... ok\ntest c9_stringtofloat_corpus ... ok\ntest c6_strtol_all_bases ... ok\ntest c8_stringtonumber_corpus ... ok\ntest c5_itoa_all_radices ... ok\ntest c10_number_coercions_exhaustive ... ok\ntest c3_grisu2_random_and_special ... ok\ntest c7_numbertostring_random_and_boundaries ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 10 passed; 0 failed; 1 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.23s\n```\n\n**11 `#[test]` functions; 10 pass, 0 fail, 1 `#[ignore]`d (documented UB probe, see below).** Cases actually compared (`MUJS_NUMBERS_STATS=1 … -- --nocapture`): C1 181, C2 114, C3 204 208, C4 807, C5 78 702, C6 3 198, C7 200 034, C8 213, C9 213, C10 300 040 (~787 k differential comparisons; f64s compared by raw bits, buffers 512 B poisoned with 0xAA and compared whole, pointers compared as offsets).\n\nI also ran a deliberate mutation self-check (compare Rust against `v*2.0`) to prove the C3 machinery is not vacuous: it reported 204 147/204 208 divergences in `len`, `K` and buffer bytes, then I reverted it.\n\n## Three harness/ABI mismatches you should know about (documented in the file header)\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs`'s `Api` table does not match `c_src/src/jsi.h` for three symbols, so I call two of them through correctly typed transmuted pointers (reading a return register the callee never set would be garbage):\n- `js_fmtexp` — real prototype is `void js_fmtexp(char*, int)` (jsdtoa.c:24, jsi.h); the table says it returns `*mut c_char`. I compare only the buffer.\n- `jsV_numbertointeger` — really returns `int` (jsvalue.c:41), not `double`.\n- `js_itoa` — really `const char *js_itoa(char *out, int v)` (jsvalue.c:167): **there is no radix parameter**, the value is always base 10. Passing a 3rd integer arg is ABI-harmless on SysV x86-64, so C5 keeps the radix sweep (2..36 plus 0/1/-1/37) — it now proves the extra argument cannot influence either side.\n\n## Excluded input classes (would kill the test process)\n\n- **`js_grisu2(±0.0)`**: for a zero significand `normalized_boundaries()` yields `m_minus.f = UINT64_MAX`, so `minus()`'s `assert(x.f >= y.f)` fires. The C `.so` is built without `-DNDEBUG` (it imports `__assert_fail`), so this is a hard `abort()` — I verified it with a standalone dlopen driver. Grisu2 is simply undefined for zero and `jsV_numbertostring` never reaches it (returns the literal `\"0\"` first). ±0 is excluded from C3 and zero-magnitude random bit patterns are skipped. `±inf`, `±NaN` and `±min-subnormal` are safe and *are* tested.\n- **`js_fmtexp` with |e| ≥ 1e9** (includes `i32::MIN`/`i32::MAX`), tested in an ignored subprocess probe.\n\n## The one real divergence found (`c4b`, `#[ignore]`d, run with `-- --ignored`)\n\nThe C's scratch array is `char se[9]`, so a 10-digit exponent writes `se[9]` out of bounds; that clobbers the adjacent loop counter `i`, and the copy-out loop then dumps ~50 bytes of raw stack (including ASLR'd pointers) into the caller's 32-byte buffer. Verbatim (truncated):\n\n```\nC4b js_fmtexp out-of-range exponents (10-digit exponent overflows the C's char se[9] — UB): 6 of 6 cases DIVERGED\n  js_fmtexp(buf, -2147483648):\n      C   : status=ExitStatus(unix_wait_status(0)) FMTEXP_RESULT last_touched_index=48 head_ascii=\"e-`......k ..........U...)............./,),(-*,(\"\n      Rust: status=ExitStatus(unix_wait_status(134)) <no result: the callee crashed or panicked>\n             [panicked at src/jsdtoa.rs:17:13: attempt to negate with overflow]\n  js_fmtexp(buf, 1000000000) / ±1000000001 / 2147483647 / -2147483647: same shape\n      Rust: [panicked at src/jsdtoa.rs:24:9: index out of bounds: the len is 9 but the index is 9]\n```\n\nBecause the C's output there is literally ASLR-dependent stack garbage, asserting on it would be flaky, so per the \"exclude classes where the C reads uninitialised memory\" rule I left the probe in place but `#[ignore]`d, with the reasoning in a doc comment. Note the Rust bound-check panic reproduces even in release (unlike the `-e` overflow panic), and the C's `se[9]` write is a genuine latent bug in `jsdtoa.c` — `jsV_numbertostring` passes a 32-byte buffer, so a caller reaching that path would get its buffer overrun. No library source was changed.\n\nHeads-up: the workspace is being edited concurrently by something else — `src/jslex.rs` (19:49), `src/regexp.rs` (19:50) and `tests/common/mod.rs` (19:38, now 757 lines vs the 735 I first read) all changed during my session. My results reflect the tree as of 19:54; the `Api` signatures I depend on were unchanged."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":986,"cache_read_input_tokens":151590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":986,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NJxrfUwvUycV6oomBiYuBt","session_id":"f3ff8386-8592-4dbd-8b83-c0778c2e2173","uuid":"15638322-04b4-4021-877b-c3d8e6ef6305","timestamp":"2026-08-14T19:54:34.971Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write dtoa/number differential tests"}
