{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5yykdspdetwjot74x4rqt6i7m6con3aefduynpxvmuq4d23stevq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final verification run is clean and stable; no other files were touched.\n\n## What was written\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hWAEAP/translated_rust/tests/scripts_lib.rs` (single new file, ~108 KB).\n\n- **13 `#[test]` functions**: `h11_regexp`, `h12_date_deterministic`, `h12b_date_clock_dependent`, `h13_json`, `h14_errors`, `h15_global_functions`, `h16_enumeration_and_prototypes`, `h17_lexing`, `h17b_lexing_unicode_escapes`, `h18_stress`, `h19_this_and_arguments`, `h20_expression_fuzz`, `h20_expression_fuzz_strict`.\n- **6264 distinct scripts** (158 + 135 + 163 + 105 + 99 + 82 + 141 + 30 + 64 + 77 + 10 + 4000 + 1200), most run in **both** sloppy and `JS_STRICT` → **14 656 `js_dostring` comparisons** across the two libraries. Plus 3 clock probes in `h12b`.\n- **Result: 11 passed, 2 failed. No crashes** — so there is no `// CRASHES:` list. (I did hit one `SIGABRT` early on, but it was a build race from running two `cargo test` processes concurrently while one was relinking `target/debug/libmujs.so`; not reproducible serially — verified over 5 subsequent runs.)\n\nTwo structural notes: `H11_SCRIPTS`/`H12_SCRIPTS`/`H19_SCRIPTS` are `const` arrays (so both modes can be driven independently), and `h17b` builds its scripts from a backslash constant because `\\uXXXX` sequences written inline get normalized before reaching the file.\n\n## Failing tests — verbatim divergences\n\n### `h11_regexp` — 1 of 158 diverged (identical in flags=0 **and** flags=1)\n\n```\n  [53] \"var r = /a/g; r.lastIndex = -1; print(r.lastIndex, r.exec('aaa'));\"\n      C   : rc=0 out=\"65535 null\\n\"\n      Rust: rc=0 out=\"0 a\\n\"\n```\n\nRoot cause: `js_Regexp.last` is `unsigned short` in both. C `jsrun.c` does `re->last = jsV_tointeger(...)` (double → `unsigned short`, which truncates to `-1 → 65535`); `src/jsrun.rs:862` does `... as u16`, and Rust's `as` **saturates**, giving `0`. `as i32 as u16` would match C.\n\n### `h12_date_deterministic` — 6 of 135 diverged (identical in flags=0 **and** flags=1)\n\n```\n  [40] \"print(new Date(NaN,0).getTime(), new Date(2020,NaN).getTime(), new Date(2020,0,NaN).getTime());\"\n      C   : rc=0 out=\"NaN NaN NaN\\n\"\n      Rust: rc=0 out=\"-62167219200000 -62167219200000 NaN\\n\"\n\n  [74] \"print(Date.UTC(2020));\"\n      C   : rc=0 out=\"NaN\\n\"\n      Rust: rc=0 out=\"-62167219200000\\n\"\n\n  [82] \"print(Date.UTC(), Date.UTC(NaN), Date.UTC(2020,NaN));\"\n      C   : rc=0 out=\"NaN NaN NaN\\n\"\n      Rust: rc=0 out=\"-62167219200000 -62167219200000 -62167219200000\\n\"\n\n  [116] \"var d = new Date(NaN); print(d.setMilliseconds(5), d.getTime());\"\n      C   : rc=0 out=\"NaN NaN\\n\"\n      Rust: rc=0 out=\"5 5\\n\"\n\n  [105] \"var S=['setFullYear','setMonth','setHours','setMinutes','setSeconds',\n                 'setUTCFullYear','setUTCMonth','setUTCHours','setUTCMinutes','setUTCSeconds'];\n           for (var i=0;i<S.length;i++) { var d = new Date(0); print(S[i], d[S[i]]()); }\"\n      C   : rc=0 out=\"setFullYear NaN\\nsetMonth NaN\\nsetHours NaN\\nsetMinutes NaN\\nsetSeconds NaN\\n\n                      setUTCFullYear NaN\\nsetUTCMonth NaN\\nsetUTCHours NaN\\nsetUTCMinutes NaN\\nsetUTCSeconds NaN\\n\"\n      Rust: rc=0 out=\"setFullYear -62167219200000\\nsetMonth -62167219200000\\nsetHours NaN\\nsetMinutes NaN\\nsetSeconds NaN\\n\n                      setUTCFullYear -62167219200000\\nsetUTCMonth -62167219200000\\nsetUTCHours NaN\\nsetUTCMinutes NaN\\nsetUTCSeconds NaN\\n\"\n\n  [104] the 14-setter x 12-value cross product (script text and both outputs are ~4 KB each;\n        the ONLY differing cells are the `NaN->` column for the four year/month setters):\n          setFullYear     C: NaN->NaN      Rust: NaN->-62167219200000\n          setMonth        C: NaN->NaN      Rust: NaN->-6216