. Find the **corresponding C code** in `c_src/src/` (same function name; the Rust is a\n   near-literal transliteration, so the C line is easy to locate).\n2. Determine the C's conversion: an explicit cast `(int)` / `(unsigned)` / `(short)` /\n   `(unsigned short)`, or an **implicit conversion** through an assignment / a function\n   parameter / a return type. Note the DESTINATION C type exactly (e.g.\n   `js_Regexp.last` is `unsigned short`, `js_Property.atts` is `int`, etc. — read `jsi.h`).\n3. Replace the Rust `x as T` with the matching `crate::cutil::d2*(x)` helper, UNLESS you can\n   prove from the surrounding code that the value is always in range and never NaN — in which\n   case LEAVE IT ALONE and record the proof in your report. Be conservative: if in doubt,\n   use the helper (the helper is identical to `as` for in-range values, so it is never wrong,\n   only occasionally redundant).\n4. Add a short `//` comment at each changed site naming the C line and the C destination type.\n\nSites needing special care (do NOT get these wrong):\n* `src/jsdate.rs:69` `Day`, `:85` `DayFromYear`, `:96` `YearFromTime`, `:173` `WeekDay`,\n  `:185/189/193/197` `HourFromTime`/`MinFromTime`/`SecFromTime`/`msFromTime`,\n  `:220/225/226` `MakeDay`, `:340/342` — compare each against `c_src/src/jsdate.c`. Several of\n  these are `return (int)(...)` where the C's return type is `int` and the argument can be\n  NaN because MuJS deliberately propagates NaN dates. `jsdate.rs:85` also has an\n  `i32` multiplication `365 * (y - 1970)` that overflows for large years — the C does the\n  same multiplication in `int`, so with `overflow-checks = false` (already set in Cargo.toml\n  for dev/test/release) it wraps identically; leave the multiplication alone.\n* `src/jsvalue.rs:96/109/111` — `jsV_numbertointeger`, `jsV_numbertoint32`. READ the C\n  (`c_src/src/jsvalue.c`) very carefully: these functions do their own NaN/infinity/range\n  handling BEFORE the cast, so the cast may already be provably in range. Do not change\n  behaviour that is already correct — but DO check the exact boundary values.\n* `src/jsvalue.rs:367` (`js_itoa`/`jsV_numbertostring` area) and `src/jsnumber.rs:85`\n  (`Np_toString` radix conversion, C destination is `uint64_t`).\n* `src/jsparse.rs:1133/1135` and `src/jsvalue.rs:109/111` implement the ToInt32 algorithm;\n  compare with the C line by line.\n* `src/jscompile.rs:195/197/648` — the C uses the cast twice, once inside a range test\n  (`num == (double)(int)num`) and once to emit the argument. Keep both faithful.\n* `src/jsdtoa.rs:344` (`k_comp`), `src/jsgc.rs:312` (`J->gcthresh`, C type `unsigned int`),\n  `src/jsrun.rs:1798` (`js_isarrayindex`, C writes through `int *k`),\n  `src/jsarray.rs:303/304` (`Ap_slice`-style clamping — the clamp may already prove\n  in-range; check whether NaN can reach it, because `NaN < 0.0` and `NaN > len` are BOTH\n  false in C and in Rust, so the `else` branch IS reachable with NaN).\n\n## Verification you must perform before finishing\n\n1. `cargo build` must succeed with no new errors.\n2. Run these two commands and paste the output verbatim in your report:\n   ```\n   cargo test --test scripts_lib h11_regexp 2>&1 | tail -30\n   cargo test --test scripts_lib h12_date_deterministic 2>&1 | tail -40\n   ```\n   Both currently FAIL (1 and 6 diverging scripts respectively). They must PASS afterwards.\n3. Then run the full suite and report the summary lines only:\n   ```\n   cargo test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test result|^running|^error|FAILED\"\n   ```\n   Report any test that regresses.\n\n## Rules\n- Modify ONLY files under `src/`. Do NOT touch `c_src/`, `tests/`, `Cargo.toml`,\n  `CONFIGS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `run_tests.sh`.\n- Do NOT change any test to make it pass.\n- The C is always right. Never \"improve\" on it.\n\nReport: a table of all 29 sites with (Rust site, C site, C destination type, action taken:\nchanged-to-d2X / left-alone + one-line justification), then the verbatim test output.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hWAEAP/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-hWAEAP-translated-rust/f3ff8386-8592-4dbd-8b83-c0778c2e2173/tasks/addbe73b3e596d31e.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
