out/stderr fd so they interfere in parallel. Pre-existing test-harness characteristics.\n- `tests/api.rs`: this file did not exist when I started — it was created at 20:17 and is still being edited by another process in this same working copy (its line numbers shifted between two consecutive runs of mine; a `tests/zz_dbg2.rs` also appeared and disappeared). Its two problems are `e7_e9_push_family_and_string_shapes`, which compares raw `js_Value` union bytes including heap pointer values and uninitialized shrstr padding (C `[64,17,2,148,…]` vs Rust `[112,11,0,148,…]` — malloc addresses, so it can never pass regardless of numeric casts), and `f16_f19_cfunctions_and_constructors`, which SIGABRTs while passing `0xDEAD` as userdata to `js_newcfunctionx`. Neither touches any float→int conversion path. Relevant to my change: that same file's `e12c_integer_conversions_via_capi` and `e14_number_coercion_helpers_direct` (which exercise `jsV_numbertointeger/int32/uint32/int16/uint16` through the C API) both pass, which independently validates the four left-alone casts in `jsvalue.rs`.\n\nOnly files under `src/` were modified: `jsarray.rs`, `jscompile.rs`, `jsdate.rs`, `jsdtoa.rs`, `jsgc.rs`, `jsnumber.rs`, `jsparse.rs`, `jsrun.rs`, `jsvalue.rs`.","usage":{"total_tokens":99546,"tool_uses":73,"duration_ms":1397717},"uuid":"28d518cb-dac7-43de-b182-90589970b082","session_id":"f3ff8386-8592-4dbd-8b83-c0778c2e2173"}
