{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jtehesbw6sjejdm3gzokrgkrkrttj3ynqqinbvbwl6aprzhlgmwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Results\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (crate root, all mechanically derived from the C):\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 237 C symbols, **0 missing** from the Rust `.so` (debug *and* release); 0 undefined non-libc imports.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — **317 rows**, all checked. 217 error call sites found by grepping every error-raising function, plus 24 resource-limit, 22 return-code-contract and 40 generic-FFI-boundary rows (NULL pointers, lengths, out-of-range enums).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — **129 rows** across 8 sections, all checked. Only **one** valid feature combination exists (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, `CMakeLists.txt` has no options); no binary target (`regexp.c`'s `main` is `#ifdef TEST`).\n\n**Test suite** — 154 tests in 11 files, all loading both `.so`s via `libloading`. Automated by `./run_tests.sh` (feature-combo loop, symbol parity, debug + release, TZ sweep).\n\n## Real translation bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **`jsY_unescape`** (`jslex.rs`) — the C's `error:` label sits *outside* the `if (jsY_accept(J,'u'))` block, so `\\q` at statement level must be a SyntaxError. Rust silently accepted it as identifier `q`.\n2. **Systemic: float→int casts** (19 sites) — Rust's `as` saturates and maps NaN to 0; C's `cvttsd2si` yields `INT_MIN`. MuJS *depends* on this: `MakeDay`'s `im = (int)m; if (im < 0 …) return NAN;` only rejects a NaN month because of it. Fixed with verified `cutil::d2i/d2l/d2u/d2s/d2us/d2ul` helpers. Broke `Date.UTC(2020)`, `new Date(NaN,0)`, 4 date setters, and `regexp.lastIndex = -1` (must store 65535, not 0), plus a `gcthresh` truncation.\n3. **`jsM_round`** (`jsmath.rs`) — C's `return -0;` is the *integer* 0 negated → `+0.0`. Rust used `-0.0`, so `1/Math.round(-0.5)` gave `-Infinity` instead of `+Infinity`.\n4. **`jsY_tokenstring[92]`** — the C literal `\"'\\'\"` is the two chars `''`; Rust had `'\\'`.\n5. **Rust panic noise on stderr** — `js_regcomp` didn't install the panic hook, so every invalid pattern printed `panicked at …`, which the C never does.\n6. **Overflow-check semantics** — set `overflow-checks = false` for dev/test so all profiles wrap like C (`js_remove(J, INT_MAX)` computes `bot + idx` *before* range-checking).\n\nAlso fixed `build.rs` to use `rustc-cdylib-link-arg` so the version script no longer breaks test-binary linking.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n- **One `#[ignore]`d probe remains** (`tests/numbers.rs::c4b`): `js_fmtexp(buf, e)` with `|e| ≥ 1e9` overflows the C's `char se[9]` and dumps ASLR'd stack bytes into the caller's buffer — there is no reproducible C behaviour to match. Every reachable input (`|e| ≤ 324`) is byte-identical; I sized the Rust scratch array at 12 so the out-of-contract inputs give a defined result rather than a panic. Documented in `ERRORS.md`'s exclusion table.\n- **The suite is not vacuous** — I mutation-tested it: changing `Runemax` by one is caught by 8 tests in 3 files; the `Math.round` and `tokenstring[92]` quirks are each caught by their own file."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":510799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1117,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3ff8386-8592-4dbd-8b83-c0778c2e2173","uuid":"2cd37889-e394-4511-99ac-cb21b37eeaf0","timestamp":"2026-08-14T20:48:46.904Z"}
